NOODLE — third-party components and data

The code in this package is under the MIT licence (LICENSE). The package contains code only. It does not include any
data set, structure prediction, model weights or analysis results.

Shipped with the package:
- 3Dmol.js 2.5.5 — BSD-3-Clause, David Koes and contributors; inlined in pipeline/report/template/report_template.html
  and therefore in every built report. Licence texts: licenses/3Dmol_LICENSE_BSD3.txt (3Dmol.js and the GLmol,
  Three.js and jQuery code it incorporates) and licenses/3Dmol_LICENSE.txt (the banner of the minified file).
  Rego N, Koes D. 3Dmol.js: molecular visualization with WebGL. Bioinformatics 2015;31:1322-4.

Used but not redistributed (install them yourself, e.g. from environments/*.yml; their own licences apply):
- ImmuneBuilder / TCRBuilder2+ (BSD-3-Clause) — structure prediction. pipeline/code/ib_patches.py patches two runtime
  issues in ImmuneBuilder 1.x by replacing two short source lines at run time; ImmuneBuilder itself is not modified or
  copied. Abanades B, et al. Commun Biol 2023;6:575.
- TCRBuilder2+ model weights — fetched by pipeline/code/fetch_weights.py through ImmuneBuilder from the URLs defined in
  the installed ImmuneBuilder release; not redistributed. Checking their terms of use is the user's responsibility.
- ANARCI (BSD-3-Clause) — IMGT numbering; HMMER (hmmscan), which ANARCI calls.
- OpenMM and pdbfixer — refinement of the predicted models.
- scanpy, anndata, harmonypy, leidenalg, umap-learn (with python-igraph and scikit-learn) — cells, states, UMAP.
- tcrdist3 (MIT) and pwseqdist, with parasail — sequence cross-check.
- STCRpy — optional Vα/Vβ hinge module.
- numpy, scipy, pandas, Biopython, h5py, freesasa, matplotlib, PyTorch.

Data:
- GEO GSE298371 (Ansaldo E, et al. PNAS 2026;123(2):e2520747122) is not included; pipeline/code/fetch_geo.py downloads
  the three supplementary files the package reads from GEO. Crystal structures for the benchmark are downloaded from the
  RCSB PDB at run time. Their terms of use apply.

Methods reimplemented here follow published work; see references/method.md and references/upstream.md for the citation
lists. Reimplementation does not imply endorsement by those authors.
